---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/');
---

<ProductLayout
  title="Kaizenly"
  description="Kaizenly — a strict, local-first focus guard."
  productName="Kaizenly"
  productBase={`${base}products/kaizenly/`}
>
  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h1>A little better, every day.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Kaizenly is a strict, local-first focus guard. Pick a time, pick the
        apps that distract you, and start a session — everything in the bag
        stays shut until the timer ends.
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: wire the download link when the release is public -->
      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <button class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Download — coming soon</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">The name</span>
      <h2>Why “Kaizenly”?</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The name comes from <strong>Kaizen</strong> — a Japanese idea meaning
        “change for the better.” <strong>Kai</strong> is change and progress;
        <strong>Zen</strong> is calm, focus, and balance; <strong>ly</strong>
        makes it a daily lifestyle; and <strong>+</strong> is the complete
        system beyond a single-feature app.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Kai</strong> — change, progress, and the decision to become better.</li>
        <li><strong>Zen</strong> — calm, focus, and balance; peaceful productivity without stress.</li>
        <li><strong>ly</strong> — a modern, daily ending that makes improvement feel natural.</li>
        <li><strong>+</strong> — a complete system, more than a single-feature app.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="lede">Together: <strong>improve your life calmly, one small step at a time.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">Focus</span>
      <h2>Pick a time. Start a session. Stay put.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        A focus session is a <strong>bag</strong> — a named set of apps that
        stays shut until the timer ends. Choose <strong>15 minutes, 45 minutes,
        3 hours, or a custom length</strong>, slide to start, and the block
        does the rest.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Bags</strong> — each session blocks a named set of distracting apps; pick 15 minutes, 45 minutes, 3 hours, or a custom duration.</li>
        <li><strong>Floating pill</strong> — a small overlay keeps the countdown on screen, so the time left is always in sight.</li>
        <li><strong>Block screen</strong> — opening a blocked app shows the block screen (Distraction Wall) and sends you back to focus.</li>
        <li><strong>Parachutes</strong> — leaving early costs parachutes, so ending a session is a deliberate decision, not a reflex.</li>
        <li><strong>A 30-minute break</strong> — with more than 30 minutes left, you can take a 30-minute break for one parachute: the clock freezes and the block returns by itself. Ending early costs more the more time is left.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">Routines &amp; streaks</span>
      <h2>Small steps, every day.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Focus works best as a <strong>routine</strong>, not a one-off effort.
        Kaizenly starts sessions on a schedule, reminds you before they begin,
        and keeps the daily target small enough to hold.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Routines</strong> — schedule sessions to start on chosen days, with a <strong>pre-alert</strong> before each one begins.</li>
        <li><strong>A one-minute daily target</strong> — one minute of focus a day is enough to keep the streak alive. Small enough to keep, every day.</li>
        <li><strong>Monday-start weeks</strong> — weeks run Monday to Sunday, so the streak counts the way your week does.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <span class="kicker">Stats</span>
      <h2>Your progress, on your device.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        Every session is recorded <strong>locally</strong>, in a Room database
        on your phone. See how your focus adds up — <strong>by day, by week,
        and by month</strong> — without anything leaving the device.
      </p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><strong>Day, week, and month views</strong> — totals for each period, side by side.</li>
        <li><strong>Post-session celebration</strong> — finishing a session ends with a small celebration, and a shareable image of the result.</li>
        <li><strong>No account, no sync</strong> — stats live in the local database; there is nothing to log in to.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="band">
        <h2>Your focus belongs to you.</h2>
        <p>
          There is <strong>no server</strong> and no custom backend. Your
          sessions and stats live in a local database on your device — no
          login, no account, and <strong>no analytics</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The only network use is Play Billing. Backups are
          <strong>local JSON files</strong> you export and import yourself —
          nothing is uploaded anywhere.
        </p>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href={`${base}products/kaizenly/privacy/`}>Read the privacy model</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container narrow">
      <p class="muted">In daily use. Privacy and Terms are already live on this site — see the links above.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>
